# ========================================
# Test Naming & Location
# ========================================

## Naming Convention

| Pattern | Jest Project | Location | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `*.spec.ts` | `unit` | `apps/api/src/**/*.spec.ts` | Unit tests, co-located with source |
| `*.integration.spec.ts` | `integration` | `apps/api/test/**/*.integration.spec.ts` | Integration tests, in test directory |

- Unit tests live **next to the file they test** (e.g., `users.service.spec.ts` beside `users.service.ts`)
- Integration tests live under `apps/api/test/` — never inside `src/`
- The `unit` project explicitly excludes `*.integration.spec.ts` to prevent overlap

## Test Directory Structure

```
apps/api/test/
├── setup/                          # Test infrastructure
│   ├── global-setup.ts             # Starts Postgres + Redis testcontainers (once)
│   ├── global-teardown.ts          # Stops containers, removes temp config (once)
│   ├── jest.setup.ts               # Per-worker: loads .env.test, overrides DB/Redis env
│   ├── worker-database.setup.ts    # Per-worker: creates DB + runs migrations
│   └── smoke.integration.spec.ts   # Verifies test infrastructure itself
├── factories/                      # Test data builders
│   ├── index.ts                    # Barrel export
│   ├── tenant.factory.ts           # createTestTenant()
│   ├── user.factory.ts             # createTestUser()
│   └── subscription.factory.ts     # createTestSubscription()
├── helpers/                        # Shared test utilities
│   ├── test-config.ts              # Testcontainer config path + types
│   ├── truncate.helper.ts          # truncateAllTables()
│   ├── redis-flush.helper.ts       # flushRedis() + resetTestState()
│   └── tenant-context.helper.ts    # withTenantContext() / withPlatformAdminContext()
└── mocks/                          # Shared mock implementations
    ├── storage.mock.ts             # MockStorageService
    └── file-type.mock.ts           # file-type ESM compatibility mock
```

# ========================================
# Integration Test Patterns
# ========================================

## Required Boilerplate

Every integration test MUST follow this structure:

```typescript
import { resetTestState } from '../helpers/redis-flush.helper';
import { createTestApp, TestApp } from '../setup/test-app.factory';

describe('YourFeature', () => {
  let app: TestApp;

  beforeAll(async () => {
    app = await createTestApp();
  }, 60000);

  beforeEach(async () => {
    await resetTestState(app.databaseService, app.redisClient);
  }, 15000);

  afterAll(async () => {
    if (app) await app.cleanup();
  }, 30000);

  it('should ...', async () => {
    // test body
  });
});
```

**Critical rules:**

- `beforeAll` timeout: **60000ms** — first call creates DB, runs migrations, boots NestJS
- `beforeEach` timeout: **15000ms** — truncates tables + flushes Redis
- `afterAll` timeout: **30000ms** — closes queues + NestJS app
- ALWAYS call `app.cleanup()` in `afterAll` — prevents Jest hanging from open connections
- ALWAYS call `resetTestState()` in `beforeEach` — ensures test isolation

## createTestApp

`createTestApp()` boots the full NestJS app with real DB and Redis. Returns `TestApp`:

```typescript
interface TestApp {
  app: INestApplication;
  module: TestingModule;         // use .get() to resolve providers
  databaseService: DatabaseService;
  redisService: RedisService;
  redisClient: Redis;            // raw ioredis
  queueProducerService: QueueProducerService;
  cleanup: () => Promise<void>;
}
```

**Auto-mocked providers:**
- `StorageService` → `MockStorageService` (no real S3/MinIO needed)
- `AuditService` → no-op mock

**Override additional providers:**

```typescript
const app = await createTestApp({
  providers: [
    { provide: SomeService, useValue: { myMethod: jest.fn() } },
  ],
});
```

## resetTestState

Truncates all transactional tables and flushes the worker's Redis DB. Reference tables survive truncation:
`plans`, `features`, `plan_entitlements`, `tenant_roles`, `tenant_permissions`, `tenant_role_permissions`, `platform_roles`, `platform_permissions`, `platform_role_permissions`.

These are populated by sync services on app boot and must not be cleared between tests.

# ========================================
# Factories
# ========================================

Use factories to create test data. All factories take a `TestingModule` and optional overrides:

```typescript
import { createTestTenant, createTestUser, createTestSubscription } from '../factories';

const tenant = await createTestTenant(app.module);
const subscription = await createTestSubscription(app.module, tenant.id);
const user = await createTestUser(app.module, { tenant_id: tenant.id });
```

## Adding New Factories

When creating a new factory:

1. Create `apps/api/test/factories/{entity}.factory.ts`
2. Export a `createTest{Entity}(module, overrides?)` function
3. Use the real repository from the module (not raw SQL)
4. Add to `apps/api/test/factories/index.ts` barrel export
5. Add integration tests for the factory in `factories.integration.spec.ts`

```typescript
// Example: apps/api/test/factories/document.factory.ts
import { TestingModule } from '@nestjs/testing';
import { DocumentRepository } from 'src/repositories/documents/document.repository';

export async function createTestDocument(
  module: TestingModule,
  overrides?: Partial<CreateDocumentRow>,
): Promise<Document> {
  const repo = module.get(DocumentRepository);
  return repo.create({
    title: 'Test Document',
    ...overrides,
  });
}
```

# ========================================
# Helpers
# ========================================

## Tenant Context Helpers

For testing RLS-protected queries:

```typescript
import { withTenantContext, withPlatformAdminContext } from '../helpers/tenant-context.helper';

// Tenant-scoped query (RLS enforced)
const rows = await withTenantContext(
  app.databaseService,
  tenantId,
  async (client) => {
    const result = await client.query('SELECT * FROM documents');
    return result.rows;
  },
  { isTenantAdmin: false },  // default
);

// Platform admin context
const rows = await withPlatformAdminContext(
  app.databaseService,
  async (client) => {
    const result = await client.query('SELECT * FROM tenants');
    return result.rows;
  },
);
```

# ========================================
# When to Write Which Type of Test
# ========================================

## Unit Tests (`*.spec.ts`)

Write unit tests for:
- Pure business logic in services (no DB calls)
- Utility functions
- DTO validation
- Mappers and transformers

Mock dependencies using Jest mocks. Co-locate with source file.

## Integration Tests (`*.integration.spec.ts`)

Write integration tests for:
- Repository operations (real DB queries)
- Service methods that interact with the database
- Factory validation
- RLS policy enforcement
- Multi-step workflows (create tenant → add user → verify permissions)
- Queue job dispatch and processing

Use `createTestApp()` + real testcontainers. Place in `apps/api/test/`.

# ========================================
# Documentation Updates
# ========================================

## When to Update Test Documentation

After writing tests, check if documentation needs updating:

### ALWAYS update when:
- Adding a new **factory** → update `apps/api/test/README.md` (factories table + directory tree) and `CONTRIBUTING.md` (directory tree)
- Adding a new **helper** → update `apps/api/test/README.md` (utilities reference + directory tree) and `CONTRIBUTING.md` (directory tree)
- Adding a new **mock** → update `apps/api/test/README.md` (directory tree) and `CONTRIBUTING.md` (directory tree)
- Adding a new **setup file** → update `apps/api/test/README.md` (architecture + directory tree)
- Changing test infrastructure (new containers, changed lifecycle) → update `apps/api/test/README.md` and `apps/api/docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` CI section

### Update Cursor rules when:
- A new test pattern is used in **3+ test files** → add to this rule
- Test directory structure changes significantly → update [project-structure.mdc](mdc:project-structure.mdc) test section

### Do NOT update docs for:
- Adding a regular test file (e.g., `users.integration.spec.ts`) — only infrastructure/shared code triggers doc updates
- Fixing or refactoring existing tests

# ========================================
# CI Requirements (Quick Reference)
# ========================================

- **Docker required** for integration tests (testcontainers manages containers)
- **Minimum Docker:** 20.10+ (testcontainers v11 requirement)
- `.env.test` is committed — no CI secrets needed
- DB/Redis connection details overridden at runtime by testcontainers
- GitHub Actions `ubuntu-latest` includes Docker — works out of the box

# ========================================
# Test Scripts
# ========================================

```bash
pnpm test                     # All tests (unit + integration)
pnpm test:unit                # Unit tests only (no Docker needed)
pnpm test:integration         # Integration tests only (Docker required)
pnpm test:integration:watch   # Integration tests in watch mode
pnpm test:coverage            # All tests with V8 coverage report
```

